The unit tests currently do not include a fail-closed regression test case to verify the behavior of the rehearsal builder when input files are missing or malformed. Adding a test case that runs `buildQuestionRuntimePayloadReadModelRehearsal` with a non-existent root or custom paths ensures that the system fails closed gracefully and records the appropriate diagnostics.

```suggestion
  test('fails closed when input files are missing or malformed', async () => {
    const {
      buildQuestionRuntimePayloadReadModelRehearsal,
    } = await import('../build-question-runtime-payload-read-model-rehearsal.mjs');

    const result = buildQuestionRuntimePayloadReadModelRehearsal({
      root: '/non-existent-path-to-force-missing-files',
      generatedAt: '2026-07-07T00:00:00.000Z',
    });

    expect(result.validatorResult.validator_status).toBe('fail');
    expect(result.validatorResult.errors).toContain('total_payload_row_count_not_3530');
    expect(result.validatorResult.errors).toContain('missing_payload_row_count_not_zero');
    expect(result.validatorResult.errors).toContain('check_failed:read_model_loads_all_3530_rows');
  });
});
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. Include fail-closed regression test cases in unit tests to verify behavior when input files are missing, malformed, or contain invalid fields, asserting that diagnostics are recorded and validation fails closed.
</details>

